{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","id":"pg_782a816958075189812412f054da5b3f","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/langwatch-scenario-release-please-md-29dea3374ef4-12f054da5b3f.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_8bcc08c454535ba2a0431e3d3861ea20"],"title":"langwatch/scenario/RELEASE_PLEASE.md @ 29dea3374ef4","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_e5a3c19708be321cfb2b10e3c6bab24f61b70f189e7116de019ca46db314ecf5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An accepted ADR replaces environment-variable configuration with per-call programmatic config: each run() gets its own EventBus, config and batchRunId, removing process-wide shared state and the need for a mutex."}],"claim_ids":["clm_e5a3c19708be321cfb2b10e3c6bab24f61b70f189e7116de019ca46db314ecf5"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","id":"pg_799ff132cc975de995a45c0b59e3196c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/langwatch-scenario-docs-adr-001-scenario-concurrency-model-md-29dea337-5c0b59e3196c.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_642eefa88dda54e9bbf9b569a6ac8f63"],"title":"langwatch/scenario/docs/adr/001-scenario-concurrency-model.md @ 29dea3374ef4","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_c70d919d7bd61b458207f87e2c464837cc45b4884c07431f2f7ea130ec6da592"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A proposed ADR moves voice STT/TTS provider state from module-global singletons to per-run ScenarioConfig.voice, because global provider state is unsafe under concurrent runs; Python still carries the global-state design."}],"claim_ids":["clm_c70d919d7bd61b458207f87e2c464837cc45b4884c07431f2f7ea130ec6da592"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","id":"pg_a0989c86058e5dadb12f397b7a057141","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/langwatch-scenario-docs-adr-002-voice-provider-state-md-29dea3374ef4-397b7a057141.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_145e81dac7af546485786655633054d8"],"title":"langwatch/scenario/docs/adr/002-voice-provider-state.md @ 29dea3374ef4","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_028099985f51dc5bce17d0da496d557abb257483a092e4079bece7c660245f6d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The JudgeAgent evaluates agent performance in real time against stated criteria at each turn, deciding whether the simulation proceeds or ends with a verdict."},{"claim_ids":["clm_068dba450ade9409355fe467ce7202c7e7891ee50b6aecef40c2ad3166cf05d6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Voice support ships platform adapters for ElevenLabs, OpenAI Realtime, Twilio Media Streams, Pipecat WebSocket and Gemini Live, with LiveKit, Vapi and generic WebRTC tracked as follow-up work."},{"claim_ids":["clm_21e0c175660cab9d8b725ef55a3c38fd3a157f2ff9850e9029692256bc265bcd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Voice surface includes scenario.audio() for injecting clips, background_noise effects, scenario.interrupt(), result.audio.save() capture, and result.latency reporting TTFB plus p50/p95."},{"claim_ids":["clm_55862db130039e88f82b05c442f3be1e8f927add7e5b1481687a7597816a4c68"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A cache_key option makes the simulated user's input repeatable for a given scenario, and a @scenario.cache decorator caches decorated calls keyed by arguments, scenario, and cache_key."},{"claim_ids":["clm_64c7a59044579d505e427546a8ccfc05eda760202ef5c28490a7fd71db34c5c4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The core entrypoint is scenario.run(), taking a name, description, agents list, optional script of steps, and optional max_turns; script steps are functions receiving the scenario state."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8ad4adc84db8c80636513c166125c588ab4243bc851216c4450407b3b29bca50"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Audio dependencies such as ffmpeg, webrtcvad and websockets ship as hard dependencies of the Python package, included in a plain pip install with no extras flag."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9ab498d6322a3f7e85de5638ef37882a8135902285b8692f80400301a3459312"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agents are integrated by implementing a single call() method, and the framework is documented as available in Python, TypeScript and Go."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cf6ae7c67e0e99424a020fbea9b3910acfab18c2fe87cfd4a8d08bde248cfd36"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The judge and user simulator rely on LLMs, so even an ElevenLabs-only voice test requires an OPENAI_API_KEY unless both are swapped via scenario.configure."},{"claim_ids":["clm_daf4e583f416bb6e19a3f09b11cbfaacf117b27af3d458bfa9457b9dab85b892"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Shipped agent components include a UserSimulatorAgent, a JudgeAgent evaluated against criteria, and a RedTeamAgent for multi-turn adversarial attacks such as Crescendo escalation with per-turn scoring and refusal detection."},{"claim_ids":["clm_de79f4f9009aa18f84d25a0ea22c8d4c9ad5c82bc42070a08d8be4ad378be12b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Scenario is described as an agent testing framework based on simulations, able to test real agent behavior by simulating users across scenarios and edge cases."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e504805d98f09534bb566fd3b02ad22a2b5ca49b769937560e4606978c0a5f9f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Debug mode shows messages step by step and allows human intervention mid-conversation; it is enabled via configure(debug=True), a per-scenario field, or the --scenario-debug pytest flag."}],"claim_ids":["clm_028099985f51dc5bce17d0da496d557abb257483a092e4079bece7c660245f6d","clm_068dba450ade9409355fe467ce7202c7e7891ee50b6aecef40c2ad3166cf05d6","clm_21e0c175660cab9d8b725ef55a3c38fd3a157f2ff9850e9029692256bc265bcd","clm_55862db130039e88f82b05c442f3be1e8f927add7e5b1481687a7597816a4c68","clm_64c7a59044579d505e427546a8ccfc05eda760202ef5c28490a7fd71db34c5c4","clm_8ad4adc84db8c80636513c166125c588ab4243bc851216c4450407b3b29bca50","clm_9ab498d6322a3f7e85de5638ef37882a8135902285b8692f80400301a3459312","clm_cf6ae7c67e0e99424a020fbea9b3910acfab18c2fe87cfd4a8d08bde248cfd36","clm_daf4e583f416bb6e19a3f09b11cbfaacf117b27af3d458bfa9457b9dab85b892","clm_de79f4f9009aa18f84d25a0ea22c8d4c9ad5c82bc42070a08d8be4ad378be12b","clm_e504805d98f09534bb566fd3b02ad22a2b5ca49b769937560e4606978c0a5f9f"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","id":"pg_f3a916a05005502ab1cae0302e4a22a2","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/langwatch-scenario-readme-md-29dea3374ef4-e0302e4a22a2.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_34db99264cff54e2817a13a0f63b1bcc"],"title":"langwatch/scenario/README.md @ 29dea3374ef4","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
